  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "getSSCertificateFingerprint",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/tls.c",
    "description": "In getSSCertificateFingerprint, the bounds check before reading a 2-byte handshake length is off by one: it allows execution when payload_packet_len > tls_record_offset+7, then performs ntohs(*(u_int16_t*)&payload[tls_record_offset+7]). This requires bytes at offsets +7 and +8, so the correct guard must ensure at least +8 is in-bounds (e.g., payload_packet_len >= tls_record_offset+9). With the current check, when tls_record_offset+8 == payload_packet_len, a 2-byte read crosses the heap buffer boundary, causing the ASan heap-buffer-overflow.",
    "conditions": "Triggered via fuzz_process_packet on crafted short/truncated TLS-like TCP payloads that drive TLS parsing into getSSCertificateFingerprint (via tlsDetectProtocolFromCertificate/ndpi_search_tls_tcp_udp) with tls_record_offset set such that payload_packet_len == tls_record_offset+8. The code then enters the non-certificate handshake branch and performs a 2-byte read at payload[tls_record_offset+7] without sufficient remaining bytes, causing OOB read."
  },
